line	<str>Climb to the roof of his house search the weather vane, use a hammer on it and search it again for 3 parts.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use each part on an anvil while holding a bronze, iron, and steel bar. There is an anvil north of his house.</str>
line	
line	<str>Put each part back on the vane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Arhein in Catherby.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Bleemadge on White Wolf Mountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sanfew in Taverley. ( if you have completed Eadgar's Ruse)</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel Tip: Use a skills necklace to teleport to the Mining Guild or use the combat bracelet to teleport to the Edgeville Monastery</str>
line	
line	<str>Gather combat gear and a weapon for killing Hammerspike's gangsters (Combat levels 44, 48, and 49)</str>
line	
line	<str>Go and talk to Hammerspike Stoutbeard in the Dwarven Mine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill his gang members, then talk to him again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Tassie Slipcast in Barbarian Village. She will give you clay. Spin it into a pot lid, then fire the pot lid in the pottery oven.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the pot lid on an empty pot. This is found in the house to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Apothecary with the pot lid and a pot. ( if you have completed A Tail of Two Cats)</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring 5 pigeon cages for the next step.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Horvik in the Varrock Armour shop.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Horvik again.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Seth Groats at the <col=800000>Lumbridge</col> chicken farm.</col>
step	66	-	Quick guide step 66
line	<str>Talk to Yanni Salika in Shilo Village (north of the bridge at the quest icon).</str>
line	
line	<str>If mining your own gems, do this now at the Shilo Village Mine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to a Jungle forester south of Shilo at the tree line (make sure to have 1 free inventory space to receive blunt axe).</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: Use the minigames teleport to Pest Control, then leave by talking to the Squire to the north and you'll be at Port Sarim. Or you Can use the Rat Pits teleport to Port Sarim, if you have completed Rat Catchers.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Brian in the Port Sarim axe shop.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Aggie in Draynor Village.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Johanhus Ulsbrecht near the prison inside of the H.A.M. Hideout.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Fred the Farmer NE of the H.A.M. Hideout at the Sheep Shearer quest start point. (4 if you haven't done Sheep Shearer)</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare a bowl of hot water and take a pot in the Lumbridge Castle kitchen if needed. Gather 3 steel bars if not already carrying.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Seth Groats in the chicken farm east of River Lum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Horvik at the armour shop in Varrock. Give him 3 steel bars.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Apothecary in Varrock south of the western bank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: amulet of glory to Edgeville, run south or use a skull sceptre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Tassie Slipcast in the Barbarian Village at the pottery icon on the minimap.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: teleport to the Mining Guild using a skills necklace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Hammerspike Stoutbeard in the most western portion of the Dwarven Mines (SW of the Ice Mountain entrance).</str>
line	
line	<str>Gather one harralander, two guam leaves, and one marrentill.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: If you have 10 Construction you can use Taverley teleport. If you're an ironman without redirect scrolls and have completed Enlightened Journey, ring of dueling to Castle Wars and take the Balloon Transport System to Taverley</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the cup of tea from the house north of Sanfew, then drink the tea to obtain an empty cup, if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sanfew on the top floor of the Taverley herblore shop about initiates. (2-2-3-1 if you have completed Eadgar's Ruse)</str>
line	
line	<str>Add your bowl of hot water to a teacup. Add a harralander, 2 guam leaves, and a marrentill. The empty bowl can be dropped afterwards.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: Ring of dueling to Al Kharid, then use the gnome glider to White Wolf Mountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Bleemadge on top of White Wolf Mountain at the gnome glider icon on the minimap.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Arhein on the Catherby docks south of the bank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight in the building north of the Seers' chapel.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: teleport to the Fishing Guild using a skills necklace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Goblin Cave south-east of the Fishing Guild. Go to the most NE room. Right-click and search the sculpture.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: Ardougne Teleport</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Wizard Cromperty in NE Ardougne at the transportation icon. ( if you have completed the Ardougne Medium Diary)</str>
line	
line	<str>You can take the hammer and chisel south of Cromperty if you didn't bring your own.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: Fishing Trawler Minigame Teleport</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Tindel Marchant on the Port Khazard south dock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring your cut gems, two of each: opal, jade, sapphire, and red topaz (can be mined with 40 Mining at Shilo Village) if you have them, otherwise, bring some gold in case you crush a gem in the upcoming step.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel tip: fairy ring teleport (AKS) or ring of dueling to Castle Wars and walk east</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rantz in the eastern Feldip Hills at the quest icon on the minimap.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Gnormadium Avlafrim west of Rantz. (at the gnome glider icon on the minimap)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search each landing light, cut the gem, and put the cut gem back. If you crush a gem, the gnome will sell you up to 2 new ones for 500 coins.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Gnormadium Avlafrim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rantz.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel Tip: Watchtower teleport run north-east. Monastery Teleport via Ardougne cloak then south-east or use Port Khazard Teleport from Lunar Spellbook, or use the minigame teleport to Fishing Trawler or fairy ring DJP and run south</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Tindel Marchant.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Wizard Cromperty in Ardougne. ( if you have completed the Ardougne Medium Diary)</str>
line	
line	<str>Take 5 pigeon cages (south of the north Ardougne bank) if needed, and get ready to fight Slagilith.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the fishing guild cave, stand in front of the sculpture and read the animate rock scroll.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the level 92 Slagilith.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the scroll again to free Petra. Make sure you finish the dialogue with her, or else you won't be able to make progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight in Seers' Village.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb to the roof of his house search the weather vane, use a hammer on it and search it again for 3 parts.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use each part on an anvil while holding a bronze, iron, and steel bar. There is an anvil north of his house.</str>
line	
line	<str>Put each part back on the vane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Arhein in Catherby.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Bleemadge on White Wolf Mountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sanfew in Taverley. ( if you have completed Eadgar's Ruse)</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel Tip: Use a skills necklace to teleport to the Mining Guild or use the combat bracelet to teleport to the Edgeville Monastery</str>
